This licence is meant to be read by a person, not a lawyer. Where the plain words and the
formal words disagree, the formal words below ("1. Permission", "2. Conditions",
"3. Reservation") are what govern.


WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
--------------------
World Dominion is a game that one person is building and intends to sell on app stores. Its
source code is published so that anyone can read it, learn from it, check the claims it
makes about its data, and build it for themselves. Publishing the source is not the same as
giving it away, and it is not the same as making it open source. This licence says exactly
what is allowed, so nobody has to guess.


1. PERMISSION
-------------
You may, free of charge:

  (a) read, study and learn from this source code;
  (b) download it and build it for your own personal, non-commercial use on a device you
      own, including on a device lent to you;
  (c) make copies for those purposes, keeping this licence with every copy;
  (d) quote short excerpts in reviews, articles, teaching material and bug reports,
      with attribution to World Dominion and its copyright holder;
  (e) use the *data* files under the terms stated for that data in
      THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md, which is not restricted by this licence (the map data is
      public domain and stays public domain).


2. CONDITIONS
-------------
Everything not expressly permitted in section 1 is reserved. In particular, you may **not**:

  (a) sell this software, or any game, app or service built from it, or charge for access
      to it, or include it in a product or bundle that is sold;
  (b) publish, distribute or share modified versions, forks, ports or re-skins — of the
      code, the artwork, the text or the game as a whole — to anyone else;
  (c) publish this software, or a build of it, on an app store, a storefront, a package
      registry or a game platform;
  (d) remove, hide or alter this licence, the copyright notice, or the attribution shown
      in the game's About screens;
  (e) use the project's name, logo or the names of its fictional factions in a way that
      suggests the copyright holder endorses or produced your work;
  (f) use the software to train, fine-tune or otherwise build a machine-learning model, or
      to generate assets for one, without written permission.

Building it yourself to play it, and telling others *where* they can read the source, are
both fine. Handing someone a copy of a build you made, or a modified copy, is not.


3. RESERVATION
--------------
The copyright holder retains all right, title and interest in the software, including all
copyright, and grants no patent, trademark or other licence except as stated in section 1.
No licence is granted to any part of the project that is not in this repository. Nothing in
this licence transfers ownership of anything to you.


4. CONTRIBUTIONS
----------------
Contributions are not being accepted at this time; see CONTRIBUTING.md. Please do not open
pull requests with code changes. If you send one anyway, the copyright holder is under no
obligation to use it, and sending it grants no rights over this project.


5. NO WARRANTY
--------------
THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED,
INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR
PURPOSE, ACCURACY OF ITS DATA, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. THE COPYRIGHT HOLDER IS NOT LIABLE FOR
ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY ARISING FROM THE SOFTWARE OR ITS USE, WHETHER IN AN
ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE. THE GAME IS A WORK OF FICTION BUILT ON PUBLIC-DOMAIN
REFERENCE DATA; NOTHING IT DISPLAYS IS A POLITICAL STATEMENT, A BORDER CLAIM OR ADVICE.


6. TERMINATION
--------------
Your permission under section 1 ends automatically if you break any condition in section 2.
On termination you must stop using the software and delete the copies you made. Sections 2
to 6 survive termination.


7. ASKING
---------
If you want to do something this licence does not allow — a licence for a school, a
translation, a video series, a commercial build — ask. A short written answer is the whole
process, and it costs nothing to ask.

Contact: the repository owner, afnan0356, through the project's repository page.


HOW THIS COMPARES TO POLYFORM STRICT
------------------------------------
PolyForm Strict 1.0.0 is the closest established licence: source-available, no commercial
use, no distribution of modified copies. This file is deliberately narrower in one place
(it also forbids redistributing *unmodified* builds, and forbids model training) and
deliberately friendlier in another (it spells out reading, learning and reviewing in plain
words). docs/SECURITY.md and the milestone report record the comparison and the
recommendation.
